## shows what an F-test with df 3,24 (4 species; 25 trials presumably)
## looks like with a test statistic of 25.65. The curve is basically
## the probability of getting a ratio of variances that you observe
## under the null model. Your test statistic is way out beyond where
## the null model is probable.
